president Trump is back in Washington  after a surprising end to his trip to  Asia he met kim jeong-hoon at the North  Korean border and became the first  sitting president to cross that frontier  north of North Korean state-run media  called it an amazing event their words  made a US lawmakers question though how  productive that meeting was in efforts  to reach a nuclear deal chip Reid is at  the White House chip what if anything  substantive came out of this meeting  well good morning you know so far there  has been no tangible progress toward any  kind of a new denuclearization deal the  parties are simply heading back to the  negotiating table after talks broke down  earlier this year and meanwhile North  Korea continues to produce material for  nuclear weapons we've agreed that we're  each going to designate a team and the  team will try and work out some details  and again speed is not the object we  want to see if we can do a really  comprehensive good deal moments before  leaving South Korea president Trump said  sanctions against North Korea are still  in place but he left open the  possibility of scaling them back some  point during the negotiations  things can happen earlier in the day  with one footstep the president made  history as the first u.s. president to  enter North Korea the impromptu meeting  unfolded after president Trump tweeted  an invitation to the North Korean leader  the day before CBS News has learned the  president didn't give his staff much of  a heads up about the tweet invitation  but he has been trying to replicate what  South Korean president moon jae-in did  when he met him at the DMZ last year but  the Kim Trump meeting wasn't the only  dramatic moment new White House press  secretary Stephane Grisham was bruised  after getting into a scuffle with North  Korean security guards who appeared to  be blocking American reporters from the  meeting room where President Trump and  Kim spoke privately for nearly an hour  back home Democratic presidential  candidates expressed concern that the  u.s. made no gains this country is no  safer when it comes to North Korea he  keeps having these summits and meetings  that  don't produce anything an initial  meeting between US and North Korean  officials is expected to happen in the  next few weeks president Trump has made  clear he wants Secretary of State Mike  Pompeo to be his lead negotiator but the  North Koreans have previously said they  don't want him anywhere near the  negotiating table meanwhile President  Trump also said he plans to invite Kim  to the White House for a meeting but  there are no details yet  Anthony chip thank you
 

